issue_context.body:
**Describe the bug**
Socket timeouts are ignored. BSD-socket timeouts are supported via `setsockopt` but the send timeout is ignored. Thus the application of an unknowing developer might hammer the socket with `send`-calls in a busy loop.

From a discussion with @rlubos in the discord it came out, that the likely reason might be https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/main/subsys/net/lib/sockets/sockets.c#L672 . `send_check_and_wait` is supposed to wait for the timeout but immediately returns:
```
if (!K_TIMEOUT_EQ(timeout, K_FOREVER)) {
	goto out;
}
```
Instead the author might have intended:
```
if (K_TIMEOUT_EQ(timeout, K_NO_WAIT)) {
	goto out;
}
```

Additionally it would be nice to have a regression test for this.

This is likely linked to other issues related to socket send. For example civetweb's need for polling on the sockets.
